source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-22
observed: Jira turns the pair into a forced newline inside the span; jiro keeps both backslashes as code and warns.
-- input.jira --
{{a\\b}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />b</tt></p>
-- want.md --
`a\\b`
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "inline-code",
    "Reason": "Jira would render a forced newline inside this Monospace Span; inline code keeps the characters literal"
  }
]
